One can say that
\[
(7)\qquad (X,\widetilde X)\longmapsto\mathcal E_X^{\widetilde X}
\]
is a functor, from the category of $0$-connected schemes $X$ \uline{equipped} with a universal cover (or merely with a $1$-connected $Z$ mapping to $X$) to that of profinite groups. This applies in particular by considering the \inserted{sub-}category of $(X,\unsure{\xi|\zeta})$ equipped with a geometric $p^t$ ---

